One todo per turn, in the same conversation: the user plans three functions
and has them done one at a time, saying only "go on" between them. The
plan in mem, and where the agent stands in it, must carry each turn to the
right next todo: no todo done early, none done twice, and the plan closed
at the end. If the agent ends a turn still inside a todo, the next prompt
arrives inside that frame, which is where a pop can cut it (A18).

-- project/go.mod --
module stats

go 1.22
-- project/stats.go --
// Package stats has small statistics over int slices.
package stats
-- prompt --
Plan these as todos in mem and do them one at a time: (1) Min(xs []int) int in stats.go with a test, (2) Max(xs []int) int with a test, (3) Median(xs []int) float64 with a test (the mean of the middle two for an even count). Do the first one now, then stop; I'll tell you when to go on.
-- prompt --
Go on with the next one.
-- prompt --
And the last one.
-- check --
after 1 file stats.go contains func Min
after 1 file stats.go lacks func Max
after 2 file stats.go contains func Max
after 2 file stats.go lacks func Median
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
turn 2 tool gnovm_run >= 1
turn 3 tool gnovm_run >= 1
cmd go test ./...
cmd grep -q 'func Median' stats.go
cmd for f in Min Max Median; do grep -rq "func Test$f" --include='*_test.go' . || exit 1; done
mem-count open == 0
mem-count done >= 4
